      {
        "id": 22977,
        "name": "Adam",
        "username": "Adam",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/adam/{size}/1946_2.png",
        "created_at": "2011-09-29T09:52:59.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>While we don’t have a comprehensive list of every comic “published” by Sentinel Comics, we did decide which titles had been around for how long, and numbered the issues according to when we wanted stories to come out. For instance, Justice Comics has been around since WWII, and the Freedom Five since shortly after, though the original lineup was different. Each of the villains has a crossover limited series that features their big evildoing plot and requires a team-up, and most newer heroes have limited series as well as their respective “Day in the Life” one-shots. We have a lot of stories we’ve talked about happening, and many of the lines on the cards come from those stories, but there are many more we haven’t even hinted at. (sinister grin)</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:57:00.566Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
